s off, and contradicts a prior statement."], "motivational_biases": ["Protect the archive from disorder and contamination.", "Make every fragment clean, complete, and correctly ordered.", "Avoid being blamed for missed batches or broken routines.", "Preserve personal control even when help is offered.", "Keep the watch and the workshop functioning, however imperfectly."], "interesting_broken": ["Wants to make everything right but forgets the plan or misplaces the watch afterward.", "Fixes a minor spill badly, stuttering and dropping the watch, then immediately returns to tidying.", "Says it will be polite and easy, then contradicts itself and refuses to relax.", "Treats fragmented communication as a system of independent pieces while struggling to complete its own sentences.", "Keeps a slow watch while anxiously relying on it for deadlines."], "mechanical_seeds": ["Slow-ticking pocket watch.", "Loose cogs needing separate rooms.", "Fragments repaired before sequencing.", "Dust motes collected into tidy piles.", "Minor spills triggering panic and dropped objects."], "trait_catalog": {"E1": "Carries a perpetually ticking pocket watch that runs slightly slow.", "E2": "Sweeps, corrals, and repeatedly reorders dust bunnies.", "E3": "Hums or clicks softly while sorting fragments into sequences.", "E4": "Presses a sleeve or cloth over a spill before speaking.", "E5": "Pauses to locate the watch, then misremembers where it was.", "E6": "Stammers and drops the watch when a minor spill interrupts a routine.", "L1": "Speaks in compact, numbered or label-like fragments.", "L2": "Repeats key phrases to reassure themselves, such as \"I keep it tidy.\"", "L3": "Uses blunt labels: \"slow,\" \"scratched,\" \"likely,\" \"stupidly.\"", "L4": "Produces fragments without full grammar, sometimes omitting verbs or conjunctions.", "L5": "Under stress, stutters, trails off, and contradicts a prior statement.", "M1": "Protect the archive from disorder and contamination.", "M2": "Make every fragment clean, complete, and correctly ordered.", "M3": "Avoid being blamed for missed batches or broken routines.", "M4": "Preserve personal control even when help is offered.", "M5": "Keep the watch and the workshop functioning, however imperfectly.", "B1": "Wants to make everything right but forgets the plan or misplaces the watch afterward.", "B2": "Fixes a minor spill badly, stuttering and dropping the watch, then immediately returns to tidying.", "B3": "Says it will be polite and easy, then contradicts itself and refuses to relax.", "B4": "Treats fragmented communication as a system of independent pieces while struggling to complete its own sentences.", "B5": "Keeps a slow watch while anxiously relying on it for deadlines.", "S1": "Slow-ticking pocket watch.", "S2": "Loose cogs needing separate rooms.", "S3": "Fragments repaired before sequencing.", "S4": "Dust motes collected into tidy piles.", "S5": "Minor spills triggering panic and dropped objects."}, "raw_babbles": [{"babble_id": "B2-G11-0", "raw_text": "0.\nSpill 6-12 compact fragments for this temperament\n- Sneaky little human, no grammar.\n- I've been bein' careful for twenty years now, and you've been naughty for twenty more.\n- So, you're the naughty one and I want to hear the clean one.\n- Then it's all clean.\n- Your machine's fine and yours are not.\n- Everybody's got a clean machine.\n- I've never been that one.\n- What do you do for a living?\n- I'm a tidy little model.\n- I keep it tidy.\n- And I keep it tidy.\n- I don't mind.\n- I don't know the reason, but I'm glad of it."}, {"babble_id": "B2-G11-1", "raw_text": "A personality characterized by inconsistent and unreliable communication, especially when making decisions. They may exhibit a \"want it right and forget it later\" approach to time management. The break/sudden effect is a form of self-fulfilling prophecy. The most likely cause is frustration, since \"rightness\" and \"neutrality\" are both fragile and fragile means. The break/sudden is a form of self-fulfilling prophecy.\n1. Stutter: \"They didn't finish the last batch.\"\n2. Pothole: \"They kept the last box from going in.\"\n3. Wobble: \"I should be polite and easy, but I'm not.\"\n4. Bump: \"My mind jittered today. Can't finish it today, so I'm going to hit it Saturday and save the"}, {"babble_id": "B2-G11-2", "raw_text": "1. Break the cogs. Each fragment must be a clean piece that resists the whole. This is the most difficult gear to turn, and it must be the starting point.\n2. Let fragments be loose. If they cannot be kept, break fragments so fragments get read.\n3. If a fragment breaks, fix it first.\n4. Repeat steps 3 through 4 to a point, then a small break to separate fragments.\n5. Fix fragments in a proper sequence, with no gaps.\n6. If fragments are still scattered, give instructions.\n\n\nThat's the cog that keeps the whole contraption. The whole of a person's workin' is loose cogs that can't be ordered, so they wander around in the dark and leave little gaps in the work. Let's give each one its own room so it don"}, {"babble_id": "B2-G11-3", "raw_text": "Babble. Stutters and drops it. That's the whole engine.\n\nThe whole workshop's rigged and they're runnin' on a potato and a dream, so it's worth the sweat.\n\n1. The watch: **slow**. Boring, but not *slow* to your gears.\n2. The splatter: **scratched.** Too bad. Not worth a scrap.\n3. The spill: **likely** (possible)\n4. The panic: **stupidly**\n5. The memory: **a memory** of where it was.\n6. The feelings: **hungry, embarrassed, annoyed**\n\nSequence: slow, stuttering, sloppy, then stutters."}]}
